// CONTAINER PARITY DEBT. Read by scripts/check-container-parity.mjs.
//
// WHAT THIS IS. The 17 azuresql-db-* skills are carried over from
// microsoft/azure-sql-database-container, not forked, and check-container-parity.mjs
// enforces that by comparing every byte of the text they ship and every field that
// must match. Every entry below is a place where this catalog KNOWINGLY DIFFERS from
// that repository, because a claim was measured and found wrong and the correction
// landed here first.
//
// EVERY ENTRY IS DEBT. It is not a settled exception, it is a promise that has not
// been kept yet. The fix belongs upstream; until the container repository takes it,
// a customer installing from the product repository still reads the wrong number.
// The check prints this list loudly on every run, green or red, for that reason.
//
// WHAT THIS IS NOT. It is not a way to make the check quieter. Three things keep it
// honest, and all three were watched failing before this file was committed:
//
//   1. A file that differs and is NOT listed here still fails the run.
//   2. A listed file that no longer differs FAILS THE RUN, saying the upstream fix
//      has landed and the entry must be deleted. An exception that outlives its
//      reason is the failure this whole check was written to remove.
//   3. An entry missing any required field fails the run. There is no partial entry.
//
// A sidecar entry lists the FIELDS it excuses, named exactly as the check reports
// them. A field of that sidecar that differs and is not named still fails.
